  "created": "2026-06-19T12:50:53.957Z",
  "description": "Standalone routing nodes for FluxFlow: switch, fork, merge, window, correlation, and join over the FluxFlow.Nodes kit, with broadcast output/error/event ports. Predicate/key extraction comes from FluxFlow.Mapping. No engine required.",
  "id": "FluxFlow.Components.Routing",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-06-19T12:54:05.993Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "yMv53YP1kGv7wLMjwcjXGhjljDvouNdhCdEW7l4qnhYptc8Tz6t0jxp/BsJk98MzsJBgWpJWS9+uwUwS9In4AQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 103788,
  "published": "2026-06-19T12:50:53.957Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuilt on the FluxFlow.Nodes kit: flow.switch/fork/window/correlation are FlowNode<TInput, ...> transforms and flow.merge is a fan-in FlowNode<TInput, TInput>, all carrying the message correlation id and timing off an injected TimeProvider; flow.join is built directly on kit primitives with two typed inputs (Left/Right), a result Output, and a Timeouts output. Each node takes its options record, key/predicate selectors (IFlowPredicate / IFlowExpressionEngine from FluxFlow.Mapping), and a TimeProvider directly. The engine factories, module, registration extensions, design-metadata provider, the definition-options reader, and the string-to-Type / expression-registry resolution layer are removed; the package depends only on FluxFlow.Nodes and FluxFlow.Mapping (runs without the engine).",
